Changelog: 14-10-2026 17:35:13

New app rpcs3-manager (BC-250 RPCS3 Manager): PS3 games on the BC-250 with the RPCS3 emulator, built like BC-250 shadPS4 Manager. Install downloads RPCS3 0.0.43-20133, the Linux build of RPCS3's v0.0.43 landmark that the app pins (rpcs3-v0.0.43-20133-53d44aa4_linux64.AppImage from RPCS3/rpcs3-binaries-linux), checks it against its SHA-256 and installs it in ~/.local/share/bc250-rpcs3-manager/emulator as rpcs3.AppImage, with "current" pointing to it; Remove takes it out, RPCS3's own folder (~/.config/rpcs3: firmware, saves, settings, installed games) stays. RPCS3's own window offers newer builds and writes them over the AppImage when asked; the app sees that by the file's size, says so in the first step and Install puts the pinned build back. When the window opens, the app asks GitHub for RPCS3's newest landmark (RPCS3/rpcs3 releases, not every build) and says when it is newer than 0.0.43, with a link; it installs only the build it was tried with. The firmware step shows the installed PS3 firmware's version (dev_flash/vsh/etc/version.txt, as RPCS3 reads it) and Install firmware… gives the user's own PS3UPDAT.PUP to RPCS3 (--installfw), with a link to PlayStation's download page; the app never downloads the firmware. Games: those installed in RPCS3's dev_hdd0/game, the disc games in RPCS3's games.yml, and the disc games (PS3_GAME beside PS3_DISC.SFB) up to five folders deep in the game folders chosen in the app (Add folder…, Remove folder…, kept in the app's settings); title, ID and version from PARAM.SFO, updates (category GD) left out, a disc game without a valid PS3_DISC.SFB shown in red, as RPCS3 does not start it. Where RPCS3 keeps its drives comes from its vfs.yml; the app reads RPCS3's files and never writes them. Play starts a game alone on the desktop (--no-gui), RPCS3 settings opens RPCS3's own window. Update Game Mode adds the ticked games to Steam as non-Steam games and takes out the others and games no longer found, with Steam closed for it and started again (core's bc250_core.steam); the artwork is drawn from the game's ICON0.PNG and PIC1.PNG, with ICON0.PNG as the logo. The shortcuts run bc250-rpcs3-run --no-gui --fullscreen "<EBOOT.BIN>": the run wrapper starts the installed RPCS3, lets the AppImage unpack itself when there is no fusermount, and, as the shadPS4 Manager's, has RPCS3 read a real controller instead of Steam's virtual one when Steam starts it, and open its windows through XWayland (QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb) when Steam starts it on a Wayland desktop. The window has its own look in RPCS3's indigo #4F34C9 (style.py). The installer uses the suite's shared venv and installs the wrapper in ~/.local/bin. The icon is a placeholder.
